{"id": "EUVD-2026-90655", "enisaUuid": "d9a5e3a8-4c9a-3c2f-8cf5-07cbfe6ee4d8", "description": "Tornado before 6.5.9 fails to limit the number of query string fields in HTTPServerRequest.__init__, allowing remote attackers to cause event-loop stalling by sending requests with thousands of query parameters. Attackers can send unauthenticated GET requests with unbounded query-string field counts to degrade response times for all clients sharing the same IOLoop.", "datePublished": "2026-10-01T10:42:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-01T14:44:26", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-3hv7-mjh2-fv65", "https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/03945136ea9746eccf61caf88edae39642e59c93", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/tornado-before-6.5.9-denial-of-service-via-query-string"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2v9w-f3h6-74rj", "CVE-2026-103261"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.47, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d79e9900-0f51-363e-b32c-5768d351727c", "product": {"name": "Tornado", "vendor": {"name": "tornadoweb"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.5.9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7f3b3af5-3032-385d-a712-4061bda4fccf", "vendor": {"name": "tornadoweb"}}], "isExploited": false}